On Sep 1, 2009, at 11:45 PM, <o.mannion at auckland.ac.nz> <o.mannion at auckland.ac.nz 
 > wrote:

> Hi,
>
> How can I send a Java long to R? The high level API only provides  
> REXPInteger, and the low-level JRI provides only rniPutIntArray. Is  
> the only way via an eval, or conversion to an int first?
>

R doesn't have anything that can represent long natively, so you have  
to convert it to either int (if 32-bit is enough), double (giving you  
about 52-bits lossless storage) or raw vector with 8-bytes for each  
long.

Cheers,
Simon

