JRIEngine does not check to see if org.rosuda.JRI.Rengine.Rengine.jriLoaded is true before instantiating a Rengine object. This means if System.getProperty("jri.ignore.ule") = true that an UnsatisfiedLinkError will be thrown on the Rengine thread and cannot be caught. I would like my application to be able to respond to this exception and prompt the user appropriately, and so I have modified the JRIEngine to check jriLoaded first and thrown an REngineException if the JRI hasn't been loaded. Can I supply this change and request it merged back into the main branch?


