On Sep 21, 2009, at 10:39 PM, Markus Loecher wrote:

> I like the default background color for the parallel coordinates  
> plot in MONDRIAN a lot. Is there any way to easily set the same bg  
> color for parallel coordinates plot in iplots ?
>

Not exactly "easily" but you can run this before creating any plots:

  `.jfield<-`("org/rosuda/ibase/Common","backgroundColor", .jnew("java/ 
awt/Color", 255L, 255L, 192L))

You can change the values (those are simply R,G,B) as you like.

Cheers,
Simon

