Hi,

(this comes from an R-help thread, but is more appropriate for this 
mailing list)

You should use this mailing list instead
http://mailman.rz.uni-augsburg.de/mailman/listinfo/stats-rosuda-devel.

Which version of rJava/JRI are you using. I am not sure this catches 
your S4 objects since I don't have readInDataAndPreprocess, etc ... but 
I think this has been fixed on this thread : 
http://article.gmane.org/gmane.comp.lang.r.rosuda.devel/791/match=s4 so 
if you have the rJava/JRI that was released after (>= 0.7-0) you should 
be fine.

In some cases, you might want to work only with the unresolved 
reference, i.e using :

r.parseAndEval( "setClass( 'track', representation(x='numeric', 
y='numeric'))" ) ;

REXPReference ref = (REXPReference)r.parseAndEval( "new('track', 1:10, 
1:10 )", r.globalEnv, false ) ;

and then work with the reference, so for example get a slot by making 
the call to the slot function:

REXPLanguage call = new REXPLanguage( new RList(new REXP[]{ new 
REXPSymbol("slot"), ref, new REXPString("x") } ) )

and then evaluate the call

r.eval( call )

Some work is being done to simplify that kind of constructs.

Romain

