On Sep 30, 2009, at 9:44 , Markus Loecher wrote:

> Dear Rserve users,
> I had assumed that Rserve was not multithreaded but it seems to spin  
> off multiple processes when faced with multiple requests ?

Yes, that's what it does (on unix). The instances are all copy-on- 
write so they share all memory initially and duplicate only modified  
pages.


> That would make it even more powerful than I initially assumed.
>

Well, that was sort of the main point - many parallel R instances ...

Cheers,
